# Op2_DrawSprBackAttrOff: the H-flipped offset (ruling 5, 2), at its first call: the sprite
# block's attribute word $38(a5) with bit 11 set (byte $38 bit 3: the object faces left), so dx is
# negated. A real state the corpus never drew through this op: Scr2_02FA0C, one of its three
# script families, sets that bit with Op2_ModSprAttr `9028` ($02FC4E, $02FC64). Every corpus call
# had it clear, so + $800 sets only bit 11.

case hflip
w a5 + $38 = {a5 + $38} + $800
